{"id":"m3-l1","title":"Multiplexers, decoders & encoders","aspect":0.5625,"wpt":960,"slides":[{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"text","box":[0.3868,0.093,0.2112,0.0853],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"Multiplexers","sz":32.0,"b":1}]}],"anchor":"t"},{"t":"text","box":[0.098,0.2408,0.8065,0.3725],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"A multiplexer circuit has a number of data inputs, one or more select inputs, and one output. It passes the signal value on one of the data inputs to the output. The data input is selected by the values of the select","sz":32.0}],"align":"just"},{"runs":[{"text":"inputs.","sz":32.0}],"align":"just"}],"anchor":"t"}]},{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"img","box":[0.2629,0.1572,0.2373,0.402],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/1.webp","crop":[0.05532,0.07912,0.04255,0.12213]},{"t":"img","box":[0.6254,0.1572,0.1802,0.4074],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/2.webp","crop":[0.14408,0.0,0.0,0.0]},{"t":"img","box":[0.1595,0.6034,0.3943,0.329],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/3.webp"},{"t":"text","box":[0.042,0.0501,0.3146,0.0942],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"2-to-1 multiplexer.","sz":36.0}]}],"anchor":"t"}]},{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"img","box":[0.1332,0.1114,0.7358,0.7938],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/4.webp"},{"t":"text","box":[0.0819,0.0313,0.2822,0.0853],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"4-to-1 multiplexer.","sz":32.0}]}],"anchor":"t"}]},{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"img","box":[0.0537,0.0546,0.6157,0.8518],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/5.webp"},{"t":"img","box":[0.5138,0.6072,0.4734,0.0776],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/6.webp"},{"t":"img","box":[0.6694,0.0427,0.2119,0.4378],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/4.webp","crop":[0.61691,0.0,0.0,0.26635]}]},{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"text","box":[0.1134,0.0861,0.8112,0.3007],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"Usually, the number of data inputs, ","sz":32.0},{"text":"n","sz":32.0,"i":1},{"text":", is an integer power of two. A multiplexer that has ","sz":32.0},{"text":"n ","sz":32.0,"i":1},{"text":"data inputs,","sz":32.0}],"align":"just"},{"runs":[{"text":"w","sz":32.0,"i":1},{"text":"0","sz":32.0},{"text":", . . . ,","sz":32.0,"i":1},{"text":"wn","sz":32.0,"i":1},{"text":"\u2212","sz":32.0},{"text":"1, requires          ","sz":32.0},{"text":" ","sz":32.0},{"text":" ","sz":32.0},{"text":" ","sz":32.0,"i":1},{"text":"select inputs and it has one output.","sz":32.0}],"align":"just"}],"anchor":"t"},{"t":"img","box":[0.4493,0.2503,0.1011,0.0624],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/7.webp"},{"t":"text","box":[0.1157,0.4463,0.809,0.3007],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"Larger multiplexers can also be constructed from smaller multiplexers. For example, the 4-to-1 multiplexer can be built using three 2-to-1 multiplexers as shown below:","sz":32.0}],"align":"just"}],"anchor":"t"}]},{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"img","box":[0.4668,0.0462,0.4007,0.8022],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/8.webp"},{"t":"text","box":[0.1866,0.8484,0.6451,0.0673],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"Using 2-to-1 multiplexers to build a 4-to-1 multiplexer.","sz":24.0}]}],"anchor":"t"},{"t":"img","box":[0.0058,0.1832,0.2736,0.5281],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/9.webp"}]},{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"text","box":[0.0306,0.4449,0.2638,0.3725],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"Similarly, 16-to-1 multiplexer can be constructed with five 4-to-1 multiplexers.","sz":32.0}]}],"anchor":"t"},{"t":"img","box":[0.4019,0.0139,0.3409,0.9861],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/10.webp"}]},{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"text","box":[0.1147,0.0532,0.7915,0.0853],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"Synthesis of Logic Functions Using Multiplexers","sz":32.0,"b":1}]}],"anchor":"t"},{"t":"img","box":[0.1424,0.207,0.6773,0.6209],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/11.webp"},{"t":"text","box":[0.0821,0.1531,0.5,0.0539],"paras":[{"runs":[{"text":"Two input XOR function using 4 to 1 multiplexer","sz":18.0,"b":1}]}],"anchor":"t"}]},{"bg":null,"items":[{"t":"img","box":[0.0941,0.293,0.1959,0.4373],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/12.webp","crop":[0.0,0.0,0.58043,0.27235]},{"t":"img","box":[0.6196,0.3662,0.3478,0.4239],"src":"/dsco/slides/m3-l1/13.webp"},{"t":"img","box":[0.4052,0.293,0.167,0.4249],"src